WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.118
Weight-space micromachines

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:03.522
Claude writes dormant

00:00:03.404 --> 00:00:04.206
implants

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:06.420
Dimitris Papailiopoulos

00:00:06.232 --> 00:00:07.481
had coding agents

00:00:07.293 --> 00:00:08.613
write small modules

00:00:08.425 --> 00:00:09.014
such as a

00:00:08.826 --> 00:00:09.710
calculator

00:00:09.793 --> 00:00:10.677
rule checkers

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:12.234
a mistake detector

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:13.295
and image eyes

00:00:13.189 --> 00:00:15.441
directly into Qwen3-0

00:00:15.253 --> 00:00:15.748
.

00:00:15.559 --> 00:00:16.632
6B's weights

00:00:16.739 --> 00:00:17.587
switched on

00:00:17.609 --> 00:00:18.834
they lift BIG-Bench

00:00:18.646 --> 00:00:21.582
Hard from 41% to 55%

00:00:21.394 --> 00:00:22.325
without RL

00:00:22.846 --> 00:00:23.966
Implants stay off

00:00:23.778 --> 00:00:24.591
until needed

00:00:24.709 --> 00:00:25.440
so the base

00:00:25.252 --> 00:00:26.466
model is bit-for-bit

00:00:26.278 --> 00:00:27.621
unchanged until one

00:00:27.433 --> 00:00:28.152
fires

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:29.578
The work builds

00:00:29.389 --> 00:00:30.816
on the 2023

00:00:30.651 --> 00:00:32.007
Looped Transformers

00:00:31.984 --> 00:00:33.552
as Programmable Computers

00:00:33.363 --> 00:00:34.825
paper and code

00:00:34.731 --> 00:00:35.886
is open source

00:00:36.414 --> 00:00:37.428
Full story on

00:00:37.239 --> 00:00:38.135
the dashboard
